## Model assets (downloaded into the local cache on first use)

### Kokoro v1.0 ONNX (`kokoro-v1.0.onnx`) and `af_heart` voice

Apache License 2.0. Copyright (c) 2024 hexgrad.
Source: https://huggingface.co/onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX

### Pocket TTS English ONNX assets

Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0). Model weights
and published speaker states are the work of Kyutai. English ONNX mirror at the
immutable revision `81b240f24f896f4cc480dc90858d1f72c9b7d64a`:
https://huggingface.co/OpenVoiceOS/phoonnx-pocket-tts

The mirror attributes the source model to `kyutai/pocket-tts`, the ONNX graph
export to `KevinAHM/pocket-tts-onnx`, and the fixed `alba` speaker state to
`kyutai/pocket-tts-without-voice-cloning`. This crate does not expose voice
cloning or user voice registration.

### Qwen3-TTS 0.6B and 1.7B GGUF

Apache License 2.0. Copyright the Qwen team (Alibaba Cloud). Fetched when the
selected model id is `qwen3-0.6` or `qwen3-1.7` (weights and speech-tokenizer
mmproj). Sources:

- https://huggingface.co/mradermacher/Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-0.6B-Base-GGUF
- https://huggingface.co/ggml-org/Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-1.7B-Base-GGUF

### Indic-Mio (`indic-mio-q8.gguf` + MioCodec decoder ONNX)

Apache-2.0 ([SPRINGLab/Indic-Mio](https://huggingface.co/SPRINGLab/Indic-Mio))
and MIT ([Aratako/MioCodec-25Hz-24kHz](https://huggingface.co/Aratako/MioCodec-25Hz-24kHz)).
This crate downloads the pinned community Q8 GGUF and ONNX decoder from
Hugging Face when the selected model id is `indic-mio`.
This crate does not redistribute those weights. The
[Indic-Mio model card](https://huggingface.co/SPRINGLab/Indic-Mio) describes
LM training data ([IndicTTS (IIT Madras)](https://www.iitm.ac.in/donlab/IndicTTS/),
among others; Rasa, Syspin, English sources on the card). Indic-Mio is
fine-tuned from [Aratako/MioTTS-0.6B](https://huggingface.co/Aratako/MioTTS-0.6B);
that base model card lists
[amphion/Emilia-Dataset](https://huggingface.co/datasets/amphion/Emilia-Dataset).
Commercial use of IndicTTS data requires an agreement with IIT Madras — check
the [IndicTTS license](https://www.iitm.ac.in/donlab/IndicTTS/license.php)
before commercial deployment. The MioCodec decoder ONNX downloaded with
indic-mio is described on
[Aratako/MioCodec-25Hz-24kHz](https://huggingface.co/Aratako/MioCodec-25Hz-24kHz);
its model card lists Emilia-YODAS (CC BY 4.0).

## Data

### Misaki English lexicons (compiled into the Kokoro grapheme-to-phoneme table)

Apache License 2.0. Copyright hexgrad.
Source: https://github.com/hexgrad/misaki
The in-process engine is `misaki-rs` (MIT), with the espeak-ng feature
disabled so the crate does not link GPL code or an extra dylib.

### FLEURS reference clips (Indic-Mio speaker embeddings)

Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).
https://huggingface.co/datasets/google/fleurs at revision
`70bb2e84b976b7e960aa89f1c648e09c59f894dd`. Precomputed 128-d MioCodec
`global_embedding` vectors from Hindi (`hi_in` ids 93 female, 695 male)
and Tamil (`ta_in` id 878 female) train clips; see
`crates/syllabix-tts/src/indic_mio/voices/SOURCE.md`.

